      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A gravida 10 para 9, after one Cesarean section (CS) followed by four vaginal deliveries was admitted at term without uterine contractions complaining of abdominal pain. The type of uterine scar was unknown. Severe bradycardia was observed at admission and an emergency Cesarean section was performed. A complete uterine rupture was revealed, the fetus in intact membranes and placenta were found in the abdominal cavity."},
